# Platform-specific Zonai build artifacts (rebuilt by compile/serve)
**/.zonai/executables/
**/.zonai/lib/

# The build-command smoke fixture generates its whole .zonai/ per run
# (tool/ci/verify_build_command.sh wipes and regenerates it, migrations
# included), unlike a real project where migrations are committed source.
e2e/build_smoke/.zonai/
# Its lock is never authoritative either: CI writes a pubspec_overrides.yaml
# into this fixture (it is not a workspace member, so the root's overrides
# miss it) and pub re-resolves against that anyway.
e2e/build_smoke/pubspec.lock

# tool/ci/run_e2e.sh does the same to every fixture it drives: it `rm -rf
# .zonai` first so a stale bundle, a leftover migration or a previous run's
# database can never satisfy an assertion the run was supposed to earn. That
# makes .zonai/ generated output for all of them, not just build_smoke -- and
# it now includes the per-mode serve logs the transport check reads.
e2e/*/.zonai/
# Same reasoning as build_smoke's, extended to the rest: run_e2e.sh runs
# `dart pub get` in each fixture, and these projects are outside the workspace
# on purpose -- that is what makes them resolve the way a user's project does.
# The four committed locks were measured stale on 2026-08-14 (revali_core
# 2.0.0 against 3.0.0, zonai_schema 0.0.0 against 0.3.1), so they were not
# pinning a reviewed resolution; they were making every run of this layer dirty
# the tree and inviting someone to commit the churn back.
e2e/*/pubspec.lock

# Runtime data (sqlite db, uploaded photos/recordings, the replay-viewer
# static build) — never source, can get large (recordings/replay-viewer
# especially), must never be committed.
**/.zonai/data/
zonai.sqlite*

# AI stuff
.llm_chat
.game_loop
# llm_chat identity for this project
.llm_chat/

# machine-local hook config (absolute paths)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Session handoff and delegation write-ups. The rest of .claude/ IS tracked on
# purpose (skills, settings), so this needs saying explicitly: these are notes
# one session leaves for another, not project history.
.claude/handoff/
apps/server/lib/gen/
# Transient output of apps/playground/test/doc_snippets_test.dart -- the test
# deletes it, but an interrupted run can leave it behind.
**/__doc_snippets__/

# showrunner: per-agent orchestration state, not source
.showrunner

# showrunner Crawler worktrees
.worktrees

# Added by saggar — local files that shouldn't be committed
.saggar/**/*.local.*
.saggar/scratchpad.md
.saggar/jobs/

# The Dart SDK the released binary and CI are pinned to (3.12.0). Kept in-tree
# so every git worktree can reach it by ABSOLUTE path without a version manager.
# See docs/dart-sdk-skew.md.
.toolchain-dart-3.12.0/
